[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says it is one issue with one fix queued. It is not. The reports merged
into it come from three different problems. One fix for the parser leaves two of them open.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Close each ticket below on its own.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

The counts come from the export at render time. They are not typed here. They follow the desk's
own view (`CauseTable`): a report is counted where it is filed. The one-day reports are filed under
`parser`, so they are counted there and again as `one-day`.

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. A date like 7 April comes out as 4 July. Most of the reports are this one. This is the fix
that is queued.

**`hint` — booking-v3 tells people to type the month first.** The booking-v3 form prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first. The form then reads the date
the tenant's way, day first. The date flips before the parser sees it. Only reports that came in
through the form of a booking-v3 tenant are this one. Fixing the parser does not fix it; the
form's hint has to change.

**`one-day` — the date moves by one day.** These reports are not a flipped month. The meeting is
on the day before or after, the same month. Some reporters saw it only in June, or saw two
different days in two cities for the same meeting. That points at time zones, not at the date
format, but these few reports are not enough to be sure. The desk already marked them as a
one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). They stay filed under `parser`, and now have their own ticket too.

## Why one ticket hid three

- Reports were merged on **subject line only** ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Every problem here uses the same words: "wrong day", "date is wrong". Matching subjects
  cannot tell them apart.
- `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. It disagrees with the
  cause for many reports (see the table), so a tag is not proof of a cause.
- The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice. Each one is counted once here.

## The same reports, by the desk's cause rules

This is the existing view from `causes.ts`. It shows `parser` and `hint`, and footnotes the
one-day reports under `parser`:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

1. Keep the parser fix on its ticket.
2. Change the booking-v3 date hint to match the tenant's locale, on its own ticket.
3. Look at time zones for the one-day reports, on their own ticket.
4. Write a new decision that replaces 0001: subject alone is not enough to merge date reports.

